                <pb facs="0547" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4998: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-22T15:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                                1927—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>207. General Feland left today Managua expecting to sail from Corinto for the
                    United States 24th when Colonel Gulick will assume command of Marine Corps in
                    Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
